  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b67d-c9f5-ab6d-3899" name="Medieval Scotland (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #94 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). 1296AD-1500AD This army list covers Scottish armies from the end of the 13th up to the end of the 15th century, before the universal adoption of the pike as the main fighting weapon of the Scottish foot soldier. During these two and a half centuries, the Scots waged war against their English neighbours in the Scottish Wars of Independence, usually unsuccessfully. The core of the Scots Common Army was the Schiltron a closely packed mass of spearmen, usually with men at arms stiffening the front ranks. The nobility after the disaster of Falkirk fought mostly dismounted, to protect themselves from the hail of arrows of the English enemy. Infantry: Schiltrons Allies: The Scots may take allies from the Medieval French army list.

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Medieval Scotland]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Characters: Up to 25% Cavalry: Up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Artillery: Up to one Cannon Allies: Up to 10%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
